---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { FEATURE_GROUPS, LEAF_PATHS } from "../lib/schema.ts";
import { REPO_URL, newProductIssueUrl, newsIssueUrl } from "../config.ts";
---
<Base title="About" description="How PresenterList works, where the data comes from and how to contribute." breadcrumbs={[{ label: "About" }]}>
  <article class="container-page mt-6 max-w-3xl space-y-10 leading-relaxed text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300">
    <header>
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-zinc-900 dark:text-white">About PresenterList</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-lg">
        PresenterList is an open, community-maintained directory of presentation software used by churches: tools for
        projecting song lyrics, scripture, slides and media. The goal is simple: help churches find the right tool without
        digging through a dozen marketing sites.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section>
      <h2 class="h-section text-zinc-900 dark:text-white">How the data works</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
        <li>Every product is a single YAML file in <a href={`${REPO_URL}/tree/main/src/data/products`} class="link">the GitHub repository</a>. The site is rebuilt from those files.</li>
        <li>Each entry lists the <strong>sources</strong> used and the date it was <strong>last verified</strong>.</li>
        <li>
          Features are only marked as supported when there's evidence. If we don't know, the feature shows as
          <strong>unknown (?)</strong> rather than guessing. Prices change often, so always check the vendor's pricing page.
        </li>
        <li>Alternatives are ranked automatically by overlap in platforms and features, not by payment. There are no sponsored listings.</li>
        <li>The full dataset is available as <a href="/products.json" class="link">JSON</a>.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="h-section text-zinc-900 dark:text-white">What we compare</h2>
      <p>
        {LEAF_PATHS.length} features in {Object.keys(FEATURE_GROUPS).length} groups. Bigger features are split into specifics, so
        "Slides" covers PowerPoint, Keynote, Google Slides, Canva, PDF and whether animations play.
        <a href="/features/" class="link">Browse all features</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="contribute">
      <h2 class="h-section text-zinc-900 dark:text-white">Contribute</h2>
      <p>Spotted something wrong or missing? There are three ways to help:</p>
      <ol class="mt-3 list-decimal space-y-2 pl-5">
        <li><a href={newProductIssueUrl} class="link">Submit a new product</a> using the GitHub issue form.</li>
        <li>Use <strong>Suggest an edit</strong> on any product page to report a correction.</li>
        <li>Open a pull request editing the product's YAML file directly. See <a href={`${REPO_URL}/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md`} class="link">CONTRIBUTING.md</a>.</li>
      </ol>
      <p class="mt-3">Vendors are welcome to correct their own listings; please include a link to a public source.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="releases">
      <h2 class="h-section text-zinc-900 dark:text-white">Releases</h2>
      <p>The <a href="/releases/" class="link">releases page</a> follows the same rules for every product:</p>
      <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
        <li>Releases are rolled up to <strong>at most one item per product per month</strong>, so products that release often don't crowd out the rest. Pre-releases and betas aren't included.</li>
        <li>Each item links to the original release notes, with a short summary. We don't republish release notes or images.</li>
        <li>Releases are collected automatically once a month from public GitHub and GitLab releases, release-note feeds and vendors' changelog pages. Summaries are written by AI (Claude) using the same instructions for every product, and checked for promotional wording before publishing.</li>
        <li>Vendors and users can <a href={newsIssueUrl} class="link">submit a release</a>. If something here is wrong, or you'd like an item removed, open an issue and we'll act on it promptly.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="h-section text-zinc-900 dark:text-white">Disclosure</h2>
      <p>
        PresenterList is maintained by the developer of <a href="/software/theopenpresenter/" class="link">TheOpenPresenter</a>.
        That product is listed using the same schema, rules and ranking as every other entry, and corrections to any listing,
        including that one, are welcome.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</Base>
